    "title": "Cameron Young's net worth: How much money the PGA golfer has made in career earnings and endorsements",
    "text": "Cameron Young's net worth: How much money the PGA golfer has made in career earnings and endorsements originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.Cameron Young is at the top of his golf game and it's paying off in a big way financially.AdvertisementThe 27-year-old captured THE PLAYERS Championship on Sunday after earning his first PGA Tour victory at the 2025 Wyndham Championship. He picked up the signature win after nailing a 375-yard drive, the longest shot ever recorded on the 18th at TPC Sawgrass - setting up a par and a 4-under 68.These wins aren't just changing his career trajectory, they're also significantly boosting his net worth and career earnings.Here's a look at what Young's net worth is in 2026 and how much money he has made on the PGA Tour.Cameron Young's career earnings have steadily climbed thanks to consistent finishes in the PGA Tour.AdvertisementThe New York native has received more than $32 million in official PGA earnings, with more than $12 million coming in from the 2026 season alone.Altogether, he's surpassed $38 million in career earnings since going pro, according to Spotrac.During the 2021-2022 season, Young became the highest-earning rookie in a season and also won the PGA Tour's Rookie of the Year award. That year, he received 94 percent of his peer's votes after finishing No. 9 in the FedEx Cup Standings and breaking into the Top 20 of the Official World Golf Rankings.READ MORE: Where is Cameron Young from? Why New York native feels right at home in Ryder Cup at Bethpage BlackCameron Young's net worth in 2026As of 2026, Young's net worth is projected to be between $17 and $18 million.AdvertisementYoung has earned millions in official prize money, thanks to multiple runner-up finishes and deep tournament runs.His breakout season in 2022, highlighted by a second-place finish at The Open Championship, helped put him on the map and significantly boosted his seven-figure income.Additional payouts from the PGA Tour's Player Impact Program have also helped boost Young's overall career earnings and net worth.Cameron Young's endorsements and sponsorship dealsBeyond his tournament prize money, Young also has additional income streams coming in from multiple brand sponsorships and endorsements.AdvertisementWhen he's not busy on the course, Young has served as a brand ambassador for Peter Millar and iCapital, among others.One of Young's newest partnerships is with retirement and wealth management company Empower, who announced in January 2026 that it had signed the PGA star to a multi-year deal.“Cam represents the next generation of excellence in professional golf,” Edmund F. Murphy III, President and Chief Executive Officer of Empower, said in a press release. \"He prepares with purpose, competes with confidence - and understands that long-term success comes from disciplined decision making. We’re proud to partner with him as he competes at the highest level.\"More lifestyle news:",
